  "details": "<p>The Barrington Atlas Directory groups this bridge with two others \"near Nepet\". This bridge is not to be confused by virtue of its modern name with \"Ponte tre Ponti\" cited in the Barrington Atlas Directory for Map 43 D3 (page 633), which lies on the Via Appia northwest of Forum Appii (BAtlas 43 D3 no. 58).</p>",
  "review_state": "published",
  "type": "FeatureCollection",
  "description": "A Roman bridge on the Via Amerina between ancient Nepet and Falerii.",
